#!/bin/bash
# Point /run/tlp-hardware.conf, which /etc/tlp.d/60-hardware.conf links to, at
# this machine's vendor settings. TLP takes a single platform profile name and
# vendors offer different ones, so the shared image picks at boot.

set -o errexit
set -o nounset
set -o pipefail

case "$(cat /sys/class/dmi/id/sys_vendor 2>/dev/null || true)" in
    "Dell Inc.") vendor=dell ;;
    Framework) vendor=framework ;;
    *) rm -f /run/tlp-hardware.conf; exit 0 ;;
esac

ln -sfn "/usr/lib/tlp-hardware/$vendor.conf" /run/tlp-hardware.conf
